  "text": "The $1.7 billion LBJ East project, starting at the I-30 interchange (including complete interchange reconstruction) and proceeding west to Greenville Road near US 75, began in 2020. All main lanes were open by early summer 2026, and as of August 2026 final work on the managed lanes was being done. A project completion ceremony took place on September 14, 2026, in conjunction with the opening of the managed lanes on the same day. (See last photo)<br /><br /> The freeway has 10 general-purpose lanes (5 each way) and 4 tolled managed lanes.<br /><br />These photos start at Interstate 30 and proceed northwest to US 75 (Central Expressway).",
